## 📄 CSV File Format

Create a CSV file named:

```text
SharedMailboxUsers.csv
```

Add the following columns and sample entries:

```csv
SharedMailbox,User
support@contoso.com,user1@contoso.com
support@contoso.com,user2@contoso.com
finance@contoso.com,user3@contoso.com
hr@contoso.com,user4@contoso.com
```

### CSV Column Explanation

- `SharedMailbox`: Email address of the shared mailbox
- `User`: Email address of the user who requires Full Access

> Replace the fictional `contoso.com` email addresses with approved addresses from your environment.

---

## 💻 PowerShell Script

Save the following script as:

```text
Add-UsersToSharedMailboxes.ps1
```

```powershell
# Connect to Exchange Online
Connect-ExchangeOnline

# Import shared mailbox and user details from CSV
$CsvPath = ".\SharedMailboxUsers.csv"

try {
    $Users = Import-Csv -Path $CsvPath -ErrorAction Stop
}
catch {
    Write-Host "Failed to import the CSV file." -ForegroundColor Red
    Write-Host $_.Exception.Message -ForegroundColor Red
    return
}

# Process every entry in the CSV file
foreach ($Entry in $Users) {

    try {
        # Validate the CSV values
        if ([string\]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($Entry.SharedMailbox) -or
            [string\]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($Entry.User)) {

            throw "SharedMailbox or User value is missing."
        }

        # Remove unnecessary spaces
        $SharedMailbox = $Entry.SharedMailbox.Trim()
        $User = $Entry.User.Trim()

        Write-Host "`nProcessing:" -ForegroundColor Cyan
        Write-Host "Shared Mailbox: $SharedMailbox"
        Write-Host "User: $User"

        # Grant Full Access permission
        Add-MailboxPermission `
            -Identity $SharedMailbox `
            -User $User `
            -AccessRights FullAccess `
            -InheritanceType All `
            -AutoMapping $false `
            -ErrorAction Stop

        Write-Host "SUCCESS: Added $User to $SharedMailbox" `
            -ForegroundColor Green
    }
    catch {
        Write-Host "FAILED: $($Entry.User) -> $($Entry.SharedMailbox)" `
            -ForegroundColor Red

        Write-Host $_.Exception.Message `
            -ForegroundColor Red
    }
}

# Disconnect from Exchange Online
Disconnect-ExchangeOnline -Confirm:$false
```

