## ▶️ How to Use the Script

### Step 1: Download or create the files

Create the following files:

```text
Add-UsersToSharedMailboxes.ps1
SharedMailboxUsers.csv
README.md
```

Keep all three files in the same folder.

---

### Step 2: Update the CSV file

Open `SharedMailboxUsers.csv` and enter the required shared mailbox and user email addresses.

Example:

```csv
SharedMailbox,User
support@contoso.com,user1@contoso.com
support@contoso.com,user2@contoso.com
finance@contoso.com,user3@contoso.com
```

Do not change the following CSV column names:

```text
SharedMailbox
User
```

---

### Step 3: Open PowerShell

Open PowerShell and navigate to the folder containing the files.

Example:

```powershell
cd "C:\Scripts\Shared-Mailbox-Bulk-Permission"
```

---

### Step 4: Run the script

Run the following command:

```powershell
.\Add-UsersToSharedMailboxes.ps1
```

---

### Step 5: Sign in to Exchange Online

When prompted, sign in using an Exchange Online administrator account with the required permissions.

---

### Step 6: Review the output

If the permission is added successfully, the script displays:

```text
SUCCESS: Added user1@contoso.com to support@contoso.com
```

If the operation fails, the script displays:

```text
FAILED: user1@contoso.com -> support@contoso.com
```

The related Exchange Online error message will appear below the failure message.

