## 🔍 Verify Full Access Permission

Use the following command to verify Full Access permissions assigned to a shared mailbox:

```powershell
Get-MailboxPermission -Identity "support@contoso.com" |
    Where-Object {
        $_.AccessRights -contains "FullAccess" -and
        $_.IsInherited -eq $false
    } |
    Format-Table User, AccessRights, Deny, IsInherited -AutoSize
```

To verify permission for one specific user:

```powershell
Get-MailboxPermission -Identity "support@contoso.com" |
    Where-Object {
        $_.User -like "*user1@contoso.com*" -and
        $_.AccessRights -contains "FullAccess"
    } |
    Format-Table User, AccessRights, Deny, IsInherited -AutoSize
```

---

## 🔄 AutoMapping Behaviour

The script uses:

```powershell
-AutoMapping $false
```

This prevents Exchange Online from automatically adding the shared mailbox to the user's Outlook profile.

If you want the shared mailbox to be added automatically to the user's Outlook profile, change it to:

```powershell
-AutoMapping $true
```

The permission command would thenAdd-MailboxPermission `
    -Identity $SharedMailbox `
    -User $User `
    -AccessRights FullAccess `
    -InheritanceType All `
    -AutoMapping $true `
    -ErrorAction Stop
```

