## 🛠️ Common Issues

### CSV file not found

Confirm that these files are stored in the same folder:

```text
Add-UsersToSharedMailboxes.ps1
SharedMailboxUsers.csv
```

You can also specify the complete CSV path:

```powershell
$CsvPath = "C:\Scripts\SharedMailboxUsers.csv"
```

---

### User or shared mailbox not found

Verify the shared mailbox:

```powershell
Get-Mailbox -Identity "support@contoso.com"
```

Verify the user:

```powershell
Get-Recipient -Identity "user1@contoso.com"
```

---

### Permission already exists

Check whether the user already has Full Access:

```powershell
Get-MailboxPermission -Identity "support@contoso.com" |
    Where-Object {
        $_.AccessRights -contains "FullAccess" -and
        $_.IsInherited -eq $false
    } |
    Format-Table User, AccessRights -AutoSize
```

---

## 🗑️ Remove Full Access Permission

Use the following command if Full Access permission must be removed:

```powershell
Remove-MailboxPermission `
    -Identity "support@contoso.com" `
    -User "user1@contoso.com" `
    -AccessRights FullAccess `
    -InheritanceType All `
    -Confirm:$false
```

Only remove the permission after confirming that the correct mailbox and user have been selected.

